# No trailing slash: `node_modules/` matches the directory only, so a SYMLINK named
# node_modules slips past it and can be committed. One was, at 0406613, pointing at its own
# absolute path — an ELOOP that breaks `node_modules/.bin` and that `git checkout` installs
# over the real (ignored) directory, uninstalling the tree's dependencies.
node_modules
dist/
bundle/
cdk.out/
*.tsbuildinfo
# Local worktrees and cleanup staging. These are checkout machinery, never product source.
/.tmp/
.cleanup-archive/
# Tool and framework caches.
.cache/
.vite/
.turbo/
.nx/cache/
.parcel-cache/
node_modules/.cache/
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example
coverage/
.nyc_output/
htmlcov/
.pytest_cache/
# Generated test and browser evidence. Curate durable screenshots under docs/design-refs/.
test-results/
test-results-*/
playwright-report/
playwright-traces/
test-logs/
test-videos/
test-screenshots/
*.test.log
test-output.txt
junit.xml
test-report.html
report.html
# Generated screenshots, capture probes, and measurements. Curated evidence belongs in
# docs/design-refs/. The existing image-generation briefs and JSONL prompt manifests are source
# records, so they remain tracked while generated images beside them stay ignored.
output/*
!output/imagegen/
output/imagegen/**
!output/imagegen/**/
!output/imagegen/**/*.md
!output/imagegen/**/*.jsonl
# Local diagnostic demo screenshots + one-off capture tooling (never committed)
.demo-screens/
# Where the browser suite writes the frames and measurements a review asks for: evidence for a
# PR body, regenerated by the run that took them, and never source. Not ignoring it also breaks
# `npm run check` outright, because the JSON a probe writes is not biome-formatted and
# `format:check` is the first link in the chain.
.qa-frames/
# What the browser suite drops beside a FAILING test: a PNG of the page at the moment of the
# failure, plus its attachment index. Regenerated on every red run and meaningless afterwards.
# Biome has no PNG or JSON-attachment handler, so ignoring these changes nothing it checks
# (665 files before and after) even though `biome.json` sets `vcs.useIgnoreFile: true`.
**/__screenshots__/
.vitest-attachments/
.check.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*.tmp
*.temp
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.worktrees/
# Nested git worktrees checked out inside the repo (each carries its own biome.json
# root config, which otherwise breaks `biome`/`npm run check` for the whole tree).
*-worktree/
.local/
# CDK deploy artifacts (account-specific / regenerated on synth+deploy)
cdk-outputs.json
cdk-deploy.log
cdk.context.json

# Local sample-size override for the diagnostic probe simulation harnesses.
engines/diagnostic/sim/sample-size.local

# The GitHub CLI resolves its config dir relative to the current working
# directory on Windows/MSYS, so running `gh auth login` from a checkout writes a
# plaintext token to ./.config/gh/hosts.yml. Keep the real one in $HOME.
.config/

# One-off local review artifacts that previously leaked into the repository root.
/changed-files.txt
/townhall-*-preview.png
